and bought stuff for your baby.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I made a subtle --

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.074
I subtly dropped a hint to you

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you should
buy me something for my baby.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I have a baby.
I need stuff."

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m like, "Okay.
All right."

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Thank you so much.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.782
Well, I´m so happy to see you
since the last time I saw you,

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know, Trump
talks about fake news a lot.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were also a victim
of fake news,

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.390
which is better than being
a victim of what this said.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
I read that you
were shot dead recently.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you shocked
when you read this?

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was, I was.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-´Cause I do the shooting.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was thrown back.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what´s weird is,
when you see that,

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.001 size:88% position:44%
you don´t know about it.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re the last person
to know about it.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.571
-Right.
-So everyone, like, phones you,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then everyone could, like,
be phoning your family.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.475
And then the weirdest is when
people send you a text going,

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Dude, are you dead?"
-Yeah.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-And I always go --

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, like, "What do you think
I´m gonna...?"

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.550
So sometimes I just don´t reply.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.218
And then, it´s like, whatever.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They slowly piece together,
"This is very bad news."

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.289
-Yeah.
But I mean, that´s the Internet.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.458 size:81% position:41%
Welcome to fake news.
-Welcome to fake news.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:00:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
You and I
are both in the business

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
of talking about politics.
-Yes.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.229
-So right now, we´re talking
about the president a lot.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-I have heard you say

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.466
that you actually relate to him
not as a politician,

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you relate
to him as a stand-up comedian.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.370
-Well, I think that´s a part
of Donald Trump I relate to.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.538 size:88% position:44%
You know, I always think

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:12.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
we try and put Donald Trump
into one box,

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think
he lives in many boxes...

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:19.712
...one of them being the box
that he´s a stand-up comedian.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.181
You probably see it in him.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he goes out,
he practices his jokes,

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.584
he works on his material.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can see him trying it out.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.554 size:78% position:39%
-Like, he´ll be like,
"What do you think?

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:28.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sheriff Arpaio?
What do you think?

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you think?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you can feel,
he´s like, "Yeah."

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the crowd cheers,
and he´s like,

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I´m working on that bit.
I´m working on that bit."

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he, like --
he, like, works the material,

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
he grows it,
he goes out there.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you can feel
when it´s starting to get old,

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, he´s like,
"Who´s gonna pay? Mexico!"

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.305
And some jokes
you feel the crowd sort of like,

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, yeah,
new jokes, new jokes.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
We get it."

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and it is true, like,
´cause "build the wall,"

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:51.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like that
was just a bit that crushed.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was it.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, now he realizes
he has to build a wall.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was just
a killer comedy bit.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, can you imagine
if we had to do the things

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
we said in our jokes.
-Exactly!

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.823
-I mean, I would be like,

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don´t want to be
a comedian anymore."

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.461
-Yeah. If Larry the Cable Guy
actually had to get ´er done...

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.030
...his life would be impossible.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.599 size:78% position:39%
Do you have any notes
on his performance?

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Look, I mean,
just work on new material.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.169
Try something new.
I was impressed with him today,

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, working with
the Democrats.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
That shook everybody up.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.407
-I was like, "Okay, okay.
That´s something different.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.775 size:81% position:41%
That´s something new."

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.177
And Republicans were like,
"Wait. I´m sorry, the what?

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
The what? The who?"

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.447
Even Democrats were like,
"You want to work with us?

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:28.615
You want to work with...?"

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, this is new.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.285
-I mean, do you think Democrats,
when that happens,

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
feels like,
"Is this some weird prank

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he reaches out
to be helpful?"

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:36.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t know.
I don´t know.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think people are just,
like, "Just do it.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just do it now
while he´s, like, here.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just do it."
-Yeah.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.196 size:75% position:38%
-Because Trump goes,
"I walk into a room,

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.731
let´s make a deal, let´s speak,"

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.299
And I think Chuck Schumer
knows him well enough.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.934
Because, I mean, they used
to hang out in New York.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he´s like,
"Yeah, let´s do it, Chuck.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.436 size:88% position:44%
Let´s just do the deal."

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.738
And then he walks out,
and he goes to the Republicans,

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
he´s like, "I made a deal.
You´re gonna love it."

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.743 size:81% position:41%
-And Mitch McConnell
probably got so angry,

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.011
his neck started wobbling.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:00.947
He was just like --
He was just like, "Waaah! Waah!"

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.382
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:04.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there is --
It´s scary.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, a lot of people
are scared by Trump,

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you do -- you see
some humor in it, as well.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.155
-Well, here´s the tough thing.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, people say to me,
they go, like,

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.791
"Why would you guys laugh?"

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two things.
First of all,

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve had, you know,
the pleasure

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I guess
I´ve been blessed enough

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.064 size:75% position:38%
to travel the world,
see many countries.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are many countries
I´ve been to

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
where people
don´t have free speech,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
and one of biggest things
that an authoritarian leader

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.671 size:88% position:44%
tries to remove from you

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the ability
to make jokes about them.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, in South Africa,
you couldn´t tell jokes

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:29.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the government
during apartheid,

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that´s something
that I cherish.

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:32.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, a person
is less frightening

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.013 size:81% position:41%
when you are laughing.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn´t diminish
what they do,

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.750 size:81% position:41%
but it´s how we cope
with these situations.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so for me, you know,
when I look at Donald Trump,

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.255 size:78% position:39%
I go, he is a paradox
for me, emotionally.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:44.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
On the one hand,
I am terrified at the notion

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.025 size:84% position:42%
that he´s the president

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the most powerful nation
in the world.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
On the other hand,
I know that I´m gonna wake up

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.129
and he´s gonna make me laugh.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, the two things...
-Yeah.

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:53.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...they co-exist.
-Yeah.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They co-exist.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, like...

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:58.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the way I put it.
This is the way --

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.406
I like to think of it like this.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:03.409
I like to think of it, like,
Donald Trump is basically --

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:06.012
He´s an asteroid
headed towards the Earth, and...

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s an asteroid,
but it´s shaped like a penis.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.516
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:13.019 size:84% position:42%
-That´s a very good way
of putting it, yeah.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it´s like, "Oh, no!"
[ Laughing ]

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly!
That´s what I want.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s all I want.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What do you --

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:22.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you are
so well-traveled,

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
what do you think
when you see him talking

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
